# TypeScript Standards

- `strict: true` + `noUnusedLocals`/`noUnusedParameters` (tsconfig.base.json). Fix type errors, never `@ts-ignore` them.
- ESM `NodeNext`: relative imports **must** carry the `.js` extension.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
import { ToolRegistry } from "./types";
// ✅ GOOD
import { ToolRegistry } from "./types.js";
```

- Internal dependencies use `workspace:*` in package.json.
- Prefer exhaustive switches with a `never` guard (see `createProvider` in `packages/providers/src/index.ts`).

## Errors

Throw typed errors, never bare strings — retry and classification logic depends on them:

```typescript
// Tools (packages/tools)
throw new ToolError("old_string not found in file", "invalid_args");
// Providers (packages/providers)
throw new LlmError(`HTTP ${res.status}: ${text}`, res.status, this.name);
```

- `ToolError` codes: `invalid_args`, `not_found`, `permission`, `timeout`, `aborted`, `runtime`. `classifyToolFailure` (`packages/core/src/toolErrors.ts`) maps them to categories and drives retryability — it reads the typed code first and only falls back to message heuristics, so throwing the right code matters more than the wording.
- `LlmError` with `status` 429 or >= 500 is retried by `withRetry` (`packages/core/src/reliability.ts`); anything else fails fast.

## Tests

Vitest, colocated: `src/foo.ts` → `src/foo.test.ts`. Required for any change to the agent loop, permissions, compaction, tools, or providers. See `testing.mdc` for how to make code testable rather than mocking around it.
